+# ── Per-build web entry routing and web identity ─────────────────────────────
+# The web build serves one unified entry document (dispatched in place between
+# the app and the landing experience) plus a dedicated landing document.
+# VITE_APP_PATH is the unified app document path; VITE_LANDING_PATH and
+# VITE_LANDING_PATH_ALIAS serve the landing document; VITE_LEGACY_PATH_REDIRECTS
+# is one "source:destination" pair for which the build generates a static
+# redirect document that preserves the query and hash. VITE_APP_NAME is the
+# public web application name (PWA manifest name) and VITE_APP_NAMESPACE
+# prefixes its offline cache identity. AGPL anti-impersonation: a redistributed
+# or forked build must carry its own NAME and NAMESPACE so it cannot install
+# over, or serve cached documents as, the original deployment's app.
+# @public VITE_LANDING_PATH
+VITE_LANDING_PATH="/landing"
+# @public VITE_LANDING_PATH_ALIAS
+VITE_LANDING_PATH_ALIAS="/landing.html"
+# @public VITE_APP_PATH
+VITE_APP_PATH="/app.html"
+# @public VITE_LEGACY_PATH_REDIRECTS
+VITE_LEGACY_PATH_REDIRECTS="/marketing.html:/landing"
+# @public VITE_APP_NAME
+VITE_APP_NAME="Natally"
+# @public VITE_APP_NAMESPACE
+VITE_APP_NAMESPACE="natally"
+
 # Public Google Analytics web-stream measurement ID for actual usage events.
 # Leave blank for an unconfigured fork; configure your own existing G- stream ID.
 # Only bounded scene/interaction metadata is sent; no account or reading content.
